A||||8||GodSend||Who put that stupid thing there!?||||1||
Z||000000||GodSend||09-27-2001||09:18 PM||||If one were to remove your radio and take a look at the hole where it goes, you would quickly see that there is a large metal - thing - sticking up from the bottom.  This -thing - is about 3 inchs tall, and rounded at the top.<P>What is its use?  How do I remove it without grinding the entire thing off?  It is getting in the way of my stereo install (its cramped back there)..Thanks guys||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||09-27-2001||09:27 PM||||It's called the rear radio support.<P>If you look at the rear of a stock Fiero radio, there is a plastic stud that is pointed to fit right into that support.<P>It is a pain to get the wiring from being crushed between the support and the rear of the radio.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>Paul Herder<BR>88 Formula - Artero kit car doner and 350 TPI<BR>86 SE - 3.2 w/440T4 Transaxle<BR>95 GMC - 350 TBI - Factory "Custom"<BR>92 Mazda Protege - Stock<BR>55 Jones - First Edition WIFE- all mods, equipment,updates :D<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||09-27-2001||09:32 PM||||The radio support bracket is riveted to the panel, so to remove it you carefully pop the rivets out and it will no longe interfere with the installation of your after market radio.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||09-27-2001||09:34 PM||||Being there done that. I just started twisting, pulling and pounding until the rivet broke. Others use a Dremel with a cutting wheel. Others a hacksaw. Whatever you do you will have the right space once you get rid of it. Good luck.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leadfoot||09-27-2001||09:47 PM||||Isn't that the structural core support for the flux capacitor?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||GodSend||09-27-2001||10:30 PM||||thanks guys.. Ill take a look on the weekend and see if I cant beat the crap out of the thing..||||reg||1
Z||000006||JetroGT||09-28-2001||12:26 AM||||Just take a flat headed screwdriver, jam it between the plastic and the bracket and give it a twist. Two rivits.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">  <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.<BR>Wanted: 86/87 Red GT, auto, pw, pl, pm, rear defrost,pt, Gray int, Spoiler. May be willing to trade the blue car.||||reg||1
Z||000007||maryjane||09-28-2001||12:35 AM||||Thought I was the only one that had trouble with that da*n thing. Too embarrassed to ask.You're sure right about getting the wires to stuff in there. Thanks guys.||||reg||14
Z||000008||Monkeyman||09-28-2001||05:38 AM||||Godsend--Don't just beat the crap out of it trying to remove it.  It seems that the plastic console support is brittle everywhere but there.  You run the risk of cracking or otherwise damaging more of the center console than just that area.  And I'm sure you know how difficult these parts are to get.  Take your time removing that.  If you don't want to completely remove the support (it is very time consuming, but easy), at least use a couple of very large, flat bladed screw drivers.  And if your console support is "perfect", email me 1<sup>st</sup> and I'd be happy to swap one of mine that isn't in great condition (but already has the stereo support removed) for your perfect one.||||reg||1
